From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 19:56:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] windows: run the module's static initializers in DllMain

Any non-ASCII byte of terminal output crashed the process with an access
violation reading 0x78, deep inside simdutf's
convert_utf8_to_utf32_with_errors. That address is a vtable slot off a
null vptr: simdutf's dispatch singleton had never been constructed.

Zig's DLL entry point does not run the module's static initializers, and
the DllMain here only brought up vcrt and acrt. Neither can help - the
.CRT$XI* and .CRT$XC* tables live in *this image*, not in the CRT. So
every namespace-scope C++ global in libghostty.dll was left zeroed:
simdutf's, and five glslang/SPIRV constructors besides.

Run them, in MSVC's own order, using the markers and helpers the static
CRT already links into the image rather than synthesizing our own.

The order is load-bearing. An earlier attempt that walked the tables
without __scrt_dllmain_before_initialize_c died in LoadLibrary with heap
corruption: that call is what initializes the module's onexit tables, and
the very first C++ initializer in the table (the standard library's
`initlocks`) calls atexit. Without it the CRT reallocs a garbage pointer
out of an uninitialized _onexit_table_t. cdb named all of this precisely;
guessing at it did not.

Verified: `wsl aptitude` (the original report), `printf` of box-drawing
characters, and CJK all run without crashing, on both the exec and the
external backends. zig build test: 3089 pass, 58 skip, 0 fail.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012ee27Fih3vSPYsqrUBpUoc
---
 src/main_c.zig | 43 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 43 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/main_c.zig b/src/main_c.zig
index 0125676d1..2b12391a1 100644
--- a/src/main_c.zig
+++ b/src/main_c.zig
@@ -260,6 +260,48 @@ pub const DllMain = if (builtin.os.tag == .windows) struct {
     const __acrt_initialize = @extern(*const fn () callconv(.c) c_int, .{ .name = "__acrt_initialize" });
     const __acrt_uninitialize = @extern(*const fn (c_int) callconv(.c) c_int, .{ .name = "__acrt_uninitialize" });
 
+    // Bringing the two CRTs up is not the whole job. A module's *static
+    // initializers* - the C++ constructors for every global in this image -
+    // live in this image, in the .CRT$XI* (C) and .CRT$XC* (C++) tables, so
+    // no amount of CRT bootstrapping runs them. MSVC's own
+    // __scrt_dllmain_crt_process_attach runs them right after the CRTs are
+    // up; Zig's DLL entry point does not, and nothing else will.
+    //
+    // Skipping them leaves every such global zeroed, which reads as a null
+    // vtable pointer at the first virtual call. simdutf is where this
+    // surfaced: its dispatch singleton is constructed this way, so the first
+    // non-ASCII byte of terminal output faulted reading 0x78 - a vtable slot
+    // off a null vptr - inside convert_utf8_to_utf32_with_errors. glslang has
+    // five more constructors in the same table.
+    //
+    // Everything below is already linked into the image by the static CRT, so
+    // this reuses the CRT's own table markers and helpers rather than
+    // synthesizing new ones. The order is MSVC's, and the order matters:
+    // __scrt_dllmain_before_initialize_c is what initializes the module's
+    // onexit tables, and an initializer that calls atexit before that (the
+    // C++ standard library's `initlocks` does, first thing) hands the CRT an
+    // uninitialized table and it reallocs a garbage pointer.
+    const PVFV = *const fn () callconv(.c) void;
+    const PIFV = *const fn () callconv(.c) c_int;
+
+    extern var __xi_a: [1]?PIFV;
+    extern var __xi_z: [1]?PIFV;
+    extern var __xc_a: [1]?PVFV;
+    extern var __xc_z: [1]?PVFV;
+
+    const _initterm = @extern(*const fn ([*]?PVFV, [*]?PVFV) callconv(.c) void, .{ .name = "_initterm" });
+    const _initterm_e = @extern(*const fn ([*]?PIFV, [*]?PIFV) callconv(.c) c_int, .{ .name = "_initterm_e" });
+    const before_initialize_c = @extern(*const fn () callconv(.c) bool, .{ .name = "__scrt_dllmain_before_initialize_c" });
+    const after_initialize_c = @extern(*const fn () callconv(.c) void, .{ .name = "__scrt_dllmain_after_initialize_c" });
+
+    fn runStaticInitializers() bool {
+        if (!before_initialize_c()) return false;
+        if (_initterm_e(&__xi_a, &__xi_z) != 0) return false;
+        after_initialize_c();
+        _initterm(&__xc_a, &__xc_z);
+        return true;
+    }
+
     pub fn handler(_: HINSTANCE, fdwReason: DWORD, _: LPVOID) callconv(.winapi) BOOL {
         // Only MSVC needs to bootstrap the CRT; MinGW handles it via dllcrt2.obj.
         if (builtin.abi != .msvc) return TRUE;
@@ -267,6 +309,7 @@ pub const DllMain = if (builtin.os.tag == .windows) struct {
             DLL_PROCESS_ATTACH => {
                 if (__vcrt_initialize() < 0) return FALSE;
                 if (__acrt_initialize() < 0) return FALSE;
+                if (!runStaticInitializers()) return FALSE;
                 return TRUE;
             },
             DLL_PROCESS_DETACH => {
